    <h2>Start with the situation, not the spreadsheet</h2>
    <p>Javanese changes with relationship and setting. <strong>Ngoko</strong> is common with close friends; <strong>Krama</strong> helps you show respect to elders, teachers, and people you have just met.</p>
    <p>When you are unsure, begin with a friendly greeting, listen to the reply, and ask what wording feels natural. These lists mark useful notes where a polite or casual alternative is especially common.</p>
